WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
- Casey Becker was born sometime&nbsp;
around 1979 or 1980. She seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.920
to be the only child in her family. Casey&nbsp;
was a fan of horror movies, just like you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.840
the viewer! I think this was an intentional&nbsp;
choice. If audiences could relate to Casey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.440
they too could feel the fear that she feels.&nbsp;
Her favorite horror movie is Halloween,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.960
which also has to be intentional, since&nbsp;
Halloween is one of the most popular horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.560
movies. She also likes the first Nightmare&nbsp;
on Elm Street but thinks the rest suck.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.400
Casey attends Woodsboro High School where she&nbsp;
had English class first period with Mrs. Tate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.080
At some point she has a short relationship&nbsp;
with her classmate Stu Macher. Not much is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.000
known about their time together. I’m not sure if&nbsp;
she became interested in horror as a result of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.240
their relationship, or if their relationship was&nbsp;
the result of their shared interest in horror.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.760
I’m gonna go with the latter, because she seems&nbsp;
to still love horror after moving on from him.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.760
Casey is not the most loyal girlfriend, she&nbsp;
always seems to be moving onto the next boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.800
so she dumps Stu to get together with&nbsp;
Steve Orth, who, according to her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.880
is big, plays football and will kick the sh*t&nbsp;
out of you. He doesn’t look that big to me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.880
but he does have a letterman jacket, so I’m&nbsp;
inclined to believe he really does play football.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.520
One night in October 1996, Casey has plans&nbsp;
to watch a couple of scary movies with Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.920
but she receives a call that changes her&nbsp;
plans. To learn who really killed Casey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.840
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.827
This video is sponsored by Audible.

00:01:10.156 --> 00:01:12.156
(metal music)

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.040
Welcome to Horror History. Go ahead and&nbsp;
just type your name into the comments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.280
because… I want to know who I’m looking at.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.440
In today’s lesson, I’ll be analyzing the&nbsp;
first Scream victim… not chronologically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.040
I believe that honor goes to Maureen Prescott…&nbsp;
but the first victim of the first movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.040
Ms. Casey Becker. Despite only appearing&nbsp;
in one sequence, Casey is easily one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.560
the most iconic Scream characters. Go to&nbsp;
a screening and you’ll see countless women&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.720
dressed up in white pullovers and blonde bob&nbsp;
cuts. Bonus points if she’s covered in blood.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.600
Casey’s psychological reaction&nbsp;
to her stalkers is interesting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.080
so let’s take it back to that fateful night.

00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:50.215
(mysterious music)

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.480
It is a foggy October night when Casey&nbsp;
is preparing for an evening of horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.680
flicks with her boyfriend. She receives&nbsp;
a phone call from an unknown caller and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.600
lets him know it’s a wrong number. Casey is&nbsp;
dressed in all white, or at least near white,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.920
from her bleach blond hair to her light faded&nbsp;
jeans. She represents a blank canvas that any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.760
horror fan could project themselves onto.&nbsp;
As a blank canvas, she’s almost tempting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.320
the killer to do a little painting. A little&nbsp;
splatter painting in red, to be more specific.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.000
The mystery caller calls back to talk, and&nbsp;
she’s amused, but hangs up on him to start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.720
some popcorn on the stove. Since Scream is a genre&nbsp;
commentary in the form of an actual horror movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.160
it makes sense that Casey is preparing some&nbsp;
popcorn at the beginning, it’s exactly where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.160
we might have been a couple minutes ago before&nbsp;
we started watching Scream, so when she gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.480
into trouble, it subconsciously put us on&nbsp;
edge as well -- it makes us share her fear.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.960
We even see the VHS player’s blue screen on her&nbsp;
TV, which if you don’t remember or aren’t old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.160
enough, is what you saw before putting&nbsp;
a tape in. This makes us feel as if we,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.560
the audience, and Casey are both going into&nbsp;
a horror movie. The mystery man calls again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.960
and now she’s genuinely curious about who it is.&nbsp;
I think she most likely believes that someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.720
she knows is messing with her, so she humors&nbsp;
him and tells him about her evening plans.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.880
- [Casey] I’m getting ready to watch a video.
- [Caller] Really? What?&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.480
-  Oh just some scary movie.
- [Caller] You like scary movies?&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.360
- Uh-huh.
- [Caller] What’s your favorite scary movie?

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.680
- We can see during this interaction, she’s&nbsp;
smiling. She’s amused by this mysterious caller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.440
and she’s kind of flirting with him. She tells&nbsp;
him her favorite is Halloween, and guesses that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.160
his might be A Nightmare on Elm St. He asks if&nbsp;
she’s got a boyfriend and she lies and says no.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.400
One of the most well-known and longstanding&nbsp;
tropes in horror is the idea that promiscuity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.640
can lead to death. We don’t see anything graphic&nbsp;
here, but we do eventually learn that she lied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.040
about being single. Since Casey was most likely&nbsp;
targeted by Stu as revenge for their break-up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.640
her infidelity serves as the offense&nbsp;
that earns her the spot as first target&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.600
in the movie. When she asks why he&nbsp;
wants to know her name, he says…

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.000
- Because I want to know who I’m looking at.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.240
- This gets her spooked and we can see her attitude&nbsp;
change. She gives him the cold shoulder and hangs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.000
up. When he calls a fourth time, she’s really&nbsp;
getting scared; we can hear it in her voice like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.080
she’s about to cry. This is when her defensive&nbsp;
instincts kick in. When the caller rings her a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.680
fifth time, she raises her voice to try to&nbsp;
intimidate him, but he just yells over her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.920
threatening to gut her like a fish if she hangs&nbsp;
up on him again. This is not her getting annoyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.480
this is her using an artificial sense of anger&nbsp;
to cover up what she’s really feeling: fear.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.880
You can tell by what she does next, she leaves her&nbsp;
burning popcorn behind to go lock all the doors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:15.200
Her response is interesting, because up to this&nbsp;
point, she has no proof that this unknown caller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.600
is even telling the truth. At this point, it could&nbsp;
be a prank call by someone miles and miles away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:24.480
so Casey’s reaction shows how insecure she really&nbsp;
is. Maybe the same kind of insecure that goes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.960
one boyfriend to the next with no gap in-between.
She threatens to call the police, but the voice on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.240
the phone tells her that they’d never make&nbsp;
it in time. This is the first confirmation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.080
that her caller maybe knows where she is&nbsp;
and this is where the tears start flowing.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.520
- [Casey] What do you want?
- [Caller] To see what your insides look like.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.880
- Next, the doorbell rings, and I think for&nbsp;
the first time, her fear is justified,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.600
because now we at least know that&nbsp;
there is someone outside her house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.280
though we don’t yet know for sure that&nbsp;
it’s her creepy caller. She yells out,

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.240
- WHO’S THERE?

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.080
- And as she’s grabbing the phone again to call&nbsp;
the police, the caller calls back to scold her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.920
saying you should never yell ‘who’s there’&nbsp;
in a horror movie. Now it’s almost 100%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.920
confirmed that the person she’s been speaking&nbsp;
with is outside her house. The killers could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.520
have started with the doorbell, but it wouldn’t&nbsp;
have been as effective as torturing her through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.560
the slow realization that the strange voice on&nbsp;
the other end of the line is no distant stranger.

00:05:13.147 --> 00:05:15.147
(huge impact)

