00:06:13.574 --> 00:06:16.543
(scary music)

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.960
Casey’s evening continues to get worse&nbsp;
as her options for survival dwindle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:24.080
She screams over the phone that her&nbsp;
boyfriend will arrive any second.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:28.560
- [Casey] He’s big and he plays football and&nbsp;
he’ll kick the sh*t out of you!

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.301
- That’s one of the best lines ever in terms&nbsp;
of acting, I get goosebumps every time.

00:06:32.301 --> 00:06:40.000
- [Caller] Ooh I’m getting scared. Shaking in my&nbsp;
boots. His name wouldn’t be… Steve would it?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.680
- He instructs her to find Steve bloodied up&nbsp;
and tied to a patio chair, and her first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.120
instinct is to go out and help him, but&nbsp;
the voice on the phone advises against it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.880
She’s forced to agree to play a game to save&nbsp;
Steve’s life, and the game is horror movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.880
trivia. She gets the first question correct, a&nbsp;
warm up question about the killer in Halloween,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:58.880
despite freezing up at first in her hysteria.&nbsp;
The second question asks for the name of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:02.720
killer in Friday the 13th, to which she&nbsp;
quickly shouts "Jason", which he deems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.040
incorrect because Mrs. Voorhees is technically&nbsp;
the killer in the original Friday the 13th.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:10.160
However, I feel like this isn’t really&nbsp;
a fair question. He asked her to name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:15.040
the killer in Friday the 13th. He did not&nbsp;
say the movie Friday the 13th. He just said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.560
Friday the 13th. Friday the 13th&nbsp;
is also the name of the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.000
and I’d say that Jason is the killer&nbsp;
of Friday the 13th the franchise.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.160
Casey is not given time to&nbsp;
make this argument though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:28.800
and she’s forced to watch Steve brutally get&nbsp;
taken out. The third and final question asks:

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.680
- [Caller] What door am I at?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.960
- Strangely, now that we know that there were&nbsp;
two killers, there’s a good chance she would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.320
have been technically correct if she had&nbsp;
just answered. I’m guessing one of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.920
probably would have been posted at each door,&nbsp;
but whatever answer she gave, the opposite door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:45.840
would be busted down. This would be their way&nbsp;
of ensuring she got that last question wrong.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.880
A fellow creator named Zack Cherry&nbsp;
actually did this really cool video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.240
where he mapped Billy and Stu’s hypothetical&nbsp;
positions outside the house throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.920
the entire scene to try to answer that&nbsp;
question: who actually ended her life?

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:02.320
- [Zack C] We have to have both of the killers on&nbsp;
either side of the house. If they were both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:07.600
on one side as people have suggested then&nbsp;
people could easily run out the opposite door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:11.280
not knowing where they are… There is no right&nbsp;
answer obviously cause they’re each at one door.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:15.600
- [Zac M] But Casey refuses to answer the final question,&nbsp;
which makes sense, because answering the questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.760
didn’t work in her favor before, and now she’s trying out&nbsp;
a new tactic. As a result, the killer at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.360
back door, which is most likely Stu, throws&nbsp;
a chair through and breaks into the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:27.200
sending Casey running to the kitchen to arm&nbsp;
herself with a knife. She actually sees Ghostface&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.960
passing through and most likely heading to&nbsp;
the front door to let his accomplice in.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.680
I think this shows that despite her shortcomings&nbsp;
in trivia, her next move is kind of intelligent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:40.000
Her attackers have made it very clear to her that&nbsp;
this is a horror movie and she is their victim.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.520
A typical horror movie victim would probably&nbsp;
run out the front door, where there would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:47.600
been someone waiting for her, but she doesn’t do&nbsp;
that, she stays in the house. She’s subverting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.760
their expectations of what goes on in a horror&nbsp;
movie. This is a preview of things to come for us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.840
as the audience of Scream, a movie that&nbsp;
constantly challenges the status quo of the genre.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.760
Casey sees her parents’ car approaching and she&nbsp;
sees Ghostface skulking around in the kitchen. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:04.400
the Zack Cherry video, he suggests that Billy went&nbsp;
upstairs and this is Stu searching the kitchen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:08.560
I agree with most of his version of the events,&nbsp;
but here’s the thing. His entire thesis relies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:12.320
on the idea that when Stu goes to the front&nbsp;
door, he lets Billy in, which we know, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.720
when Casey’s parents get back, the door is left&nbsp;
open, and then Billy goes up and Stu stays down.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:20.400
We never see this on camera. I feel like they&nbsp;
just as easily could have done the opposite:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.320
Stu could have gone up and Billy could have&nbsp;
stayed down. So from a positioning standpoint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.880
it’s basically 50-50 on who the killer is. I’m&nbsp;
also not convinced that either of them even goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:33.680
upstairs, because after she sees this, the next&nbsp;
time she looks into the house, she sees this:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:37.600
Ghostface with his back to the window, and then&nbsp;
he suddenly whips around and spots her. To me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.360
this looks more like one of them was turned away&nbsp;
from the window to talk to the other, and when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.360
Casey appeared at the window, she was spotted, and then the other one said something along the lines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:49.600
of “behind you” and that’s what caused this guy&nbsp;
by the window to spin around so quickly like that.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:54.000
But CZ! This is an analysis of Casey&nbsp;
Becker, why are you analyzing Ghostface??&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.080
Because what happens next changes&nbsp;
how I look at Casey's final moments.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.920
After being spotted she runs out of the house&nbsp;
barefoot, but Ghostface quickly catches her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.320
sticks a knife through her chest&nbsp;
and proceeds to strangle her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:08.080
Still she manages to fight back by kicking him&nbsp;
off of her. It's actually really impressive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.640
both Stu and Billy are over 6 feet tall&nbsp;
to her 5'4" and she sends him flying back.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:17.120
Just then, Casey's parents are returning home, but&nbsp;
in a Halloween II moment, she isn't able to call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:21.040
out to them, but I think this has more to do with&nbsp;
her vocal cord being damaged when she was choked.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.600
They go inside and she struggles&nbsp;
to get to the front porch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.360
where her attacker pins her down. At this&nbsp;
point she knows she has no chance to survive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.680
so instead of fighting back with the last of&nbsp;
her energy, she reaches up to remove the mask.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:35.040
I think she knows this wasn't a random attack,&nbsp;
because at this point it's pretty clear that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.480
was someone who is familiar with her house and&nbsp;
it's layout, and somewhat familiar with her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.680
enough to know she would be home alone&nbsp;
and her boyfriend was on the way over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:46.080
So she might as well learn who was after her&nbsp;
before it's all over. To satisfy her curiosity.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:50.880
A lot is made of her reaction to seeing the&nbsp;
face. To me, this is not a face of surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:55.840
but one of recognition. I believe Stu is the&nbsp;
one to deal the finishing blow. You can map out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:00.000
their routes through the house or analyze her&nbsp;
expression all you want, but to me, it always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.240
had to be Stu who would have wanted dibs to get&nbsp;
revenge on his disloyal ex-girlfriend -- the girl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.160
he most likely spent nights enjoying horror&nbsp;
movies with would become the victim of one.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.640
She actually doesn't die right away&nbsp;
when he stabs her on the porch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.840
so her mom goes inside and actually&nbsp;
hears Casey die over the phone.

00:11:14.067 --> 00:11:15.353
- [Mrs. Becker] Oh my God,  I can hear her!

00:11:15.353 --> 00:11:15.853
(Casey moaning)

00:11:15.854 --> 00:11:16.354
- [Stu] Tree!

00:11:16.553 --> 00:11:18.232
(busy signal)

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:22.160
- It was kind of a missed opportunity actually. If&nbsp;
she had just said the name of her killer when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:26.160
